+        { "ref": "ea03b8b91:.metaproject/flows/448-2026-10-14-review-run-keepalive/description.md", "says": "'the head gate checks that commit without being loosened' and 'a head that is not the pull request's head still fails the gate' — i.e. passing the PR's current head was expected to pass" },
+        { "ref": "src/review/managed.ts:1051-1053", "says": "explicit warning when --head replaces the recorded head: a deliberate choice to allow replacement" }
+      ],
+      "reasoning": "--head is deliberate, for a recorded-wrong-head recovery, and the flow intended the gate to be unchanged. The finding is right that nothing checks the claimed head was the one reviewed, so naming the PR's current head silences the moved check — which the flow's own observation treats as success. But the suggested fix (equal to or ancestor of the recorded head) would refuse the documented recovery case, where the actually reviewed commit is typically newer than the stale recorded one. Whether that recovery should need an operator act is a product choice.",
+      "question": "`review complete --head` exists to fix a wrongly recorded head, and it can also silence the moved-head check. Keep it warning-only, gate a differing --head behind an operator act, or restrict it to the recorded head's ancestors (which drops the recovery case)?",
+      "options": ["keep — warning-only replacement, as flow 448 decided", "uphold with a different fix — a --head that differs from the recorded head needs an operator card/TTY", "uphold as written — accept only the recorded head or an ancestor, dropping the flow 448 recovery case"]
+    },
+    {
+      "finding_id": "A-04",
+      "verdict": "downgraded",
+      "severity": "minor",
+      "intent_signals": [
+        { "ref": "src/review/managed.ts:1106", "says": "comment: the waiver replaces the research gate's refusal and 'the checklist below still names it' — computeReadiness runs right after (managed.ts:1111-1112) and refuses on any non-waived failing item" },
+        { "ref": "src/review/readiness.ts:309-312", "says": "ledger item re-runs researchErrors() over research.json" },
+        { "ref": "src/review/readiness.ts:212-219", "says": "reviewers item re-runs dispatchErrors() and the coverage gate" },
+        { "ref": "docs/docs/guides/review-with-a-record.md:797", "says": "the drop only happens after an operator-quoted readiness waiver ('Only you can waive an item')" }
+      ],
+      "reasoning": "Most of what the wholesale drop removes is re-checked by readiness for every item that was not waived, so the 'every research error is dropped' impact is mostly compensated by design. What genuinely escapes is the integrity part of packageResearchErrors that readiness does not repeat (artifact-locator checks and the manifest/research.json dispatch mismatch, research.ts:121-132), and only after a human waiver. A real but narrower defect."
+    },
+    {
+      "finding_id": "A-05",
+      "verdict": "upheld",
+      "reasoning": "No intent signal that publish should skip the tamper or evidence-level checks: d5f5f9dec says publish is 'held by the same checklist', but those two checks live outside the checklist (managed.ts:1039, 1075-1082) and publishReview never calls them (publish.ts:146-171). Publish does require the operator to read the body (review.ts:4892-4909), which surfaces a missing evidence line but not a tampered round record. --partial is a deliberate path for not-ready packages; the shared gate must keep it."
+    },
